WEBVTT

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:06.140
In the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit, Amen.

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:13.620
The reading from the Sinaxadion for September 10th, on which we commemorate the most pious

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:17.380
empress, Pulcheria.

00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:24.340
The memory of the most pious empress, Pulcheria, who died in peace.

00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:33.700
And Pulcheria was the sister of Emperor Thodosios II in the years 408 to 450.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:39.300
On the death of Arcadia's, the administration of the empire, felt to her, although she was

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:41.980
only 15 years old.

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:49.540
She saw to it that the young Thodosius and his two other sisters, Arcadia and Maria, were

00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:53.780
brought up in godliness and modesty.

00:00:53.860 --> 00:01:00.500
She encouraged her sisters to remain in lifelong virginity as she did herself.

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:09.500
On the death of Thodosios, she married the Emperor Marcian in the years 450 through 457.

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:18.260
A good man, a no longer young, with whom she lived in chastity, with the same love of godliness

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:21.860
and the same dedication to the church.

00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:28.420
Throughout her life, she expended the most part of her wealth in charitable works and was

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:36.260
a zealous builder of churches, hospitals, orphanages and monasteries.

00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:43.260
Her zeal in preserving the purity of the Orthodox faith was just as ardent.

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:51.540
The fourth ecumenical council met at Calcedon in her reign to anathematize utikis and the

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:58.920
monophysites, and during its sessions she took her place with Marcian in the midst of the

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:01.100
Holy Fathers.

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:12.580
She died in peace at the age of 54, in the year 453 through the prayers of our Holy Fathers

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:18.460
O Lord, Jesus Christ our God, have mercy on us and save us.
